@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 240
title Agent-First Orchestration

package "Specialist Agents (gpt-4o-mini)" {
  component "QA Agent\nretrieve_local_context" as QAAgent #lightgreen
  component "Web Agent\nweb_search" as WebAgent #lightblue
  component "Quiz Agent\ngenerate_quiz tool" as QuizAgent #lightpink
  component "Note Agent\nsummarize/create notes" as NoteAgent #lightcyan
  component "Ingestion Agent\ningest_corpus" as IngestionAgent #lightyellow
  component "Routing Agent\nLLM fallback router" as RoutingAgent #lightgray
}

component "Orchestrator Agent\n(TutorAgent)" as Orchestrator #orange
component "QuizService\n(Core Logic)" as QuizService #pink

actor User
User --> Orchestrator : "create 20 quizzes\nfrom documents"\n"create study notes"

Orchestrator --> RoutingAgent : LLM fallback\n(when deterministic fails)
Orchestrator --> QAAgent : STEM questions\n(math, physics, CS, etc.)
Orchestrator --> WebAgent : Current events\nhistory, arts
Orchestrator --> QuizAgent : Quiz requests\n(extract count & topic)
Orchestrator --> NoteAgent : Note/summary requests
Orchestrator --> IngestionAgent : File uploads
QuizAgent --> QuizService : generate_quiz tool call

QAAgent --> User : Answer with\nlocal citations [1][2]
WebAgent --> User : Answer with\nURL citations
QuizAgent --> User : Interactive quiz\n(3-40 questions)
NoteAgent --> User : Study notes\n(saved to file)
IngestionAgent --> User : Ingestion summary
RoutingAgent --> Orchestrator : Routing decision\n(JSON response)

note right of Orchestrator
  Agent-First Quiz Generation:
  
  Routing Rules:
  • Math/Science/Tech → qa_agent
  • News/Current → web_agent
  • "create N quizzes" → quiz_agent
  • "create notes/summarize" → note_agent
  • Upload → ingestion_agent
  • Fallback → routing_agent (LLM)
  
  Count Extraction:
  "create 20 quizzes" → count=20
  "quiz me" → count=4 (default)
  "10 questions on topic" → count=10
  
  Topic Extraction:
  From: user message, uploaded docs, context
  
  FORBIDDEN: Answering quiz requests with text
  REQUIRED: ALWAYS call appropriate tool/agent
end note

note right of NoteAgent
  Note Agent:
  
  • Document summarization
  • Study note generation
  • Text file creation
  • Source-filtered retrieval
  • Saves notes to filesystem
  
  Features:
  • Summarizes uploaded documents
  • Creates structured study notes
  • Saves to data/generated/notes/
  • Supports source filtering
end note

note left of QuizAgent
  Quiz Agent:
  
  • Calls generate_quiz function tool
  • Tool parameters:
    - topic: str (broad, searchable)
    - count: int (3-40, enforced)
    - difficulty: Optional[str]
  • Uses QuizService for generation
  • Stores quiz in AgentState
  • Supports source filtering
  • Topic/count extracted from context
  
  Called by orchestrator agent
end note

@enduml

@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 240
title Quiz Generation with Source Filtering

actor Learner
component "Orchestrator Agent" as Orchestrator
component "Quiz Agent" as QuizAgent
component "QuizService" as QuizService
component "Retriever" as Retriever
component "VectorStore" as VectorStore
component "OpenAI API\n(gpt-4o-mini)" as OpenAI
component "ProgressTracker" as ProgressTracker
database "LearnerProfile\n*.json" as Profile
folder "Uploaded Files" as UploadedFiles

Learner -> Orchestrator : "create 20 quizzes\nfrom uploaded document"
Orchestrator -> Orchestrator : Extract:\n• count=20\n• source_filter=["doc.pdf"]
Orchestrator -> QuizAgent : Route to quiz agent
QuizAgent -> QuizAgent : Call generate_quiz tool
QuizAgent -> QuizService : generate_quiz(topic, count, source_filter)

QuizService -> QuizService : Calculate max_tokens:\n(20 × 150) + 500 = 3500
QuizService -> Retriever : Find content\n+ source_filter
Retriever -> VectorStore : Search ONLY uploaded files\n(320x faster!)
VectorStore -> UploadedFiles : Filter by filename
VectorStore --> Retriever : Top chunks from uploads
Retriever --> QuizService : Relevant passages

QuizService -> OpenAI : Generate 20 questions\nmax_tokens=3500
OpenAI --> QuizService : Quiz with 20×4 choices
QuizService --> QuizAgent : Return quiz object
QuizAgent --> QuizAgent : Store in AgentState
QuizAgent --> Orchestrator : Return quiz via state
Orchestrator --> Learner : Display interactive quiz

Learner -> Orchestrator : Submit answers [0,2,1,3...]
Orchestrator -> Orchestrator : evaluate_quiz(quiz, answers)\n(via TutorAgent)
Orchestrator -> QuizService : evaluate_quiz(quiz, answers)
QuizService -> QuizService : Grade answers
QuizService -> ProgressTracker : Update profile (score, topic)

ProgressTracker -> Profile : Load profile
ProgressTracker -> ProgressTracker : Calculate deltas based on score
ProgressTracker -> Profile : Save updated profile

QuizService --> Learner : Results + feedback\n+ explanations

note right of QuizService
  Dynamic Token Calculation:
  
  max_tokens = (num_questions × 150) + 500
  
  Examples:
  • 4 questions → 1,100 tokens
  • 20 questions → 3,500 tokens
  • 40 questions → 6,500 tokens
  
  Prevents JSON truncation!
end note

note left of VectorStore
  Source Filtering:
  
  Without filter:
  • Searches all 10,000 chunks
  • Old docs rank higher
  • Slower, less relevant
  
  With filter ["lecture9.pdf"]:
  • Searches only 31 chunks
  • 320x faster!
  • 100% relevance
  • Guaranteed from user's file
end note

note bottom of ProgressTracker
  Profile Updates Based on Score:
  
  ≥70% (Strong):
    +0.12 domain strength
    -0.08 domain struggle
    difficulty = "independent challenge"
  
  40-69% (Moderate):
    +0.06 domain strength
    no struggle change
    difficulty = "guided practice"
  
  <40% (Struggling):
    +0.02 domain strength
    +0.10 domain struggle
    difficulty = "foundational guidance"
  
  Also updates:
  • concepts_mastered[domain] += correct_count
  • total_time_minutes += (questions × 1.5)
  • next_topics based on weak areas
end note

@enduml

@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 220
title Document Upload & Auto-Ingestion

actor User
component "Streamlit UI\n(Chat & Learn tab)" as UI
component "IngestionAgent" as IngestionAgent
component "IngestionPipeline" as Ingestion
component "Parsers\n(PDF, Markdown, TXT)" as Parsers
component "Chunker" as Chunker
component "EmbeddingClient\n(sentence-transformers)" as EmbeddingClient
component "VectorStore\n(ChromaDB with domain collections)" as VectorStore
component "ChunkJsonlStore" as ChunkStore
database "ChromaDB\n(data/vector_store)" as ChromaDB
database "chunks.jsonl\n(data/processed)" as ChunksFile

User --> UI : Upload PDF in chat
UI -> UI : Store filename for filtering
User --> UI : Send first message
UI --> IngestionAgent : Auto-trigger ingestion
IngestionAgent --> Ingestion : ingest_file(pdf_path)
Ingestion --> Parsers : Parse PDF
Parsers --> Chunker : Extract text by page
Chunker --> Chunker : Create 500-token chunks\n80-token overlap
Chunker --> EmbeddingClient : Batch encode
EmbeddingClient --> VectorStore : Store vectors\n+ source metadata
VectorStore --> ChromaDB : Persist to domain collections\n(ai_tutor_{domain})
Ingestion --> ChunkStore : Save full chunks
ChunkStore --> ChunksFile : Append JSONL

IngestionAgent --> UI : Summary: N chunks indexed
UI --> User : "Ready! Try:\n'create 20 quizzes from this'"

note right of VectorStore
  ChromaDB with Domain Collections:
  
  • Separate collections per domain
  • Collection name: ai_tutor_{domain}
  • Metadata includes:
    - source_path: "data/uploads/lecture9.pdf"
    - filename: "lecture9.pdf"
    - domain: math/physics/cs/etc.
  
  Source Filtering:
  • Query with source_filter=["lecture9.pdf"]
  • Only searches matching chunks
  • 320x faster, 100% relevant
  • Pre-filters by filename before similarity
end note

note left of Chunker
  Smart chunking:
  • Preserves paragraphs
  • Maintains context with overlap
  • Tracks document metadata
  • Page numbers for citations
  • Source path for filtering
end note

note bottom of UI
  Simplified Workflow:
  
  1. Upload PDF in chat
  2. Say "create 20 quizzes from this"
  3. Take quiz immediately!
  
  Features:
  • Auto-ingestion on first message
  • Source filtering enabled
  • Interactive quiz interface
  • Markdown export available
end note

@enduml

@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 240
title Note Generation Workflow

actor User
component "Streamlit UI\n(Chat & Learn)" as UI
component "Orchestrator Agent" as Orchestrator
component "Note Agent" as NoteAgent
component "Retriever" as Retriever
component "VectorStore" as VectorStore
component "OpenAI API\n(gpt-4o-mini)" as OpenAI
database "Uploaded Documents" as Docs

User --> UI : Upload PDF in chat
User --> UI : "create study notes\nfrom uploaded documents"

UI --> Orchestrator : Natural language request
Orchestrator --> Orchestrator : Detect note intent\n(summarize, notes, text file)
Orchestrator --> NoteAgent : Route to note agent

NoteAgent --> Retriever : Retrieve document content\n(with source filter)
Retriever --> VectorStore : Search uploaded files
VectorStore --> Retriever : Relevant chunks
Retriever --> NoteAgent : Document passages

NoteAgent --> OpenAI : Generate structured notes\nwith document context
OpenAI --> NoteAgent : Formatted study notes

NoteAgent --> NoteAgent : Save to filesystem\n(data/generated/notes/)
NoteAgent --> Orchestrator : Return note summary
Orchestrator --> UI : Display notes + file path
UI --> User : Show study notes\n+ download link

note right of NoteAgent
  Note Generation:
  
  • Summarizes uploaded documents
  • Creates structured study notes
  • Saves to filesystem
  • Supports source filtering
  • Multiple formats (markdown, text)
  
  Features:
  • Document-based content
  • Organized by topic/section
  • Includes citations
  • Auto-saved to files
end note

note left of Retriever
  Source Filtering:
  
  • Searches only uploaded files
  • 320x faster retrieval
  • 100% relevance
  • Guaranteed from user's documents
end note

@enduml

@startuml Component_Communication
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 240
title Component Communication Patterns

package "Service Layer" {
    component "TutorService\n(Singleton)" as Service
    component "Session Event\nProcessing" as EventProc
}

package "Core System" {
    component "TutorSystem\n(Facade)" as System
    component "TutorAgent\n(Orchestrator)" as Agent
}

package "Specialist Agents" {
    component "QA Agent" as QA
    component "Web Agent" as Web
    component "Quiz Agent" as Quiz
    component "Note Agent" as Note
    component "Ingestion Agent" as Ingestion
    component "Routing Agent" as Routing
}

package "Shared State" {
    component "AgentState\n(Mutable Container)" as State
}

package "Infrastructure" {
    component "Retriever" as Retriever
    component "VectorStore\n(ChromaDB)" as VectorStore
    component "LLM Client" as LLM
    component "SQLiteSession" as Session
    component "QuizService" as QuizService
}

Service --> System : answer_question()\ncreate_quiz()\nprocess_event()
System --> Agent : answer()\ndelegate to orchestrator
Agent --> State : Initialize/reset\nfor each query

Agent --> Routing : LLM fallback routing\n(when deterministic fails)
Agent --> QA : Route STEM questions
Agent --> Web : Route current events
Agent --> Quiz : Route quiz requests
Agent --> Note : Route note requests
Agent --> Ingestion : Route uploads

QA --> Retriever : retrieve_local_context()
Retriever --> VectorStore : cosine search\n+ source filter
QA --> LLM : generate cited answer
QA --> State : Store results\n(last_hits, last_citations)

Web --> LLM : synthesize web results
Web --> State : Store results\n(last_source = "web")

Quiz --> QuizService : generate_quiz tool call
QuizService --> Retriever : retrieve with source filter
QuizService --> LLM : generate questions\n(dynamic max_tokens)
Quiz --> State : Store quiz\n(last_quiz)

Note --> Retriever : retrieve document content
Note --> LLM : generate summary
Note --> State : Store results

Ingestion --> VectorStore : add chunks
Ingestion --> State : Store ingestion summary

Routing --> Agent : Return routing decision\n(JSON with route, confidence)

Agent --> State : Collect all results
Agent --> Agent : Format TutorResponse
Agent --> Session : Save conversation turn
Agent --> System : Return TutorResponse
System --> Service : Return TutorResponse

note right of State
  AgentState Pattern:
  
  Purpose:
  • Enable inter-agent communication
  • Centralize result collection
  • Loose coupling between agents
  
  Fields:
  • last_hits: List[RetrievalHit]
  • last_citations: List[str]
  • last_source: Optional[str]
  • last_quiz: Optional[Quiz]
  
  Lifecycle:
  1. Reset at query start
  2. Agents write results
  3. Orchestrator reads results
  4. Reset for next query
end note

note left of Agent
  Routing Strategy:
  
  1. Deterministic Routing:
     • Keyword-based rules
     • Fast, no LLM calls
     • Confidence = 1.0
  
  2. LLM-Based Routing:
     • Fallback when deterministic fails
     • Structured JSON output
     • Confidence threshold: 0.45
  
  Routing Targets:
  • "qa": STEM questions
  • "web": Current events
  • "quiz": Quiz generation
  • "note": Summaries/notes
  • "ingestion": File uploads
  
  Routing Agent:
  • LLM-based fallback router
  • Returns structured JSON
  • Confidence threshold: 0.45
  • Used when deterministic fails
end note

note bottom of Service
  Service Layer Responsibilities:
  
  • Abstraction between UI and core
  • Session event processing
  • Source-filtered retrieval
  • Context formatting
  • Error handling
  • MCP connection caching
  • Tool list caching
end note

@enduml
